# Project

Personal Chrome MV3 extension for Jira Cloud (`your-site.atlassian.net`). It builds a collapsible blocking tree (epic children + inward Blocks links) on issue pages and in the side panel.

Keep changes small and in the existing layout: `src/shared/` for logic, `src/ui/` for React, `src/content/` for Jira DOM, `src/background/` for the service worker.

## Do

- Use the Jira session cookie. Fetch with `credentials: "include"` and `X-Atlassian-Token: no-check`.
- Honor `MAX_TREE_DEPTH` and `MAX_TREE_NODES` in `src/shared/constants.ts`.
- Batch Jira key lookups (`key in (...)`, 50 keys per request). Prefetch breadth-first, one level at a time.
- Keep the content-script drawer in a shadow root so Jira CSS does not leak in.
- Re-attach the header launcher when Jira re-renders (`src/content/mountPoints.ts`).

## Do not

- Add OAuth, PATs, API tokens, or new Jira host permissions.
- Use `--disable-extensions-except` with `npm run chrome`.
- Put panel styles in Jira's document CSS (except the small launcher in `content.css`).
- Expand `ISSUE_FIELDS` without a reason; extra fields cost every search.
